  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.25,
      "end_seconds": 6.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "hi there, is it alright if I come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.72,
      "end_seconds": 10.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.6,
      "end_seconds": 16.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "well, I've been having pain low in the pelvis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.37,
      "end_seconds": 24.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "And when did that that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.72,
      "end_seconds": 31.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "I mean, ever since... since last weekend, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.36,
      "end_seconds": 34.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "and how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.66,
      "end_seconds": 38.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "I'd call it moderate"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.07,
      "end_seconds": 42.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Mhm. Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.93,
      "end_seconds": 59.52,
      "duration_seconds": 14.59,
      "text": "it usually comes with bloating the, The bloating? That's been for two days as for bloating, maybe a six out of ten on a bad day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.63,
      "end_seconds": 73.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "and what about burning when passing urine, missed period or vaginal discharge?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.12,
      "end_seconds": 78.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "None, uh, as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.45,
      "end_seconds": 80.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Nothing like fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.51,
      "end_seconds": 84.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Not that I've noticed, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.99,
      "end_seconds": 87.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Okay, so. Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.97,
      "end_seconds": 91.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "So, no, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.47,
      "end_seconds": 98.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.39,
      "end_seconds": 102.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Okay, so no, no allergies to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.39,
      "end_seconds": 109.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.45,
      "end_seconds": 115.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Well, um, no, I don't take anything regularly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.03,
      "end_seconds": 121.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.48,
      "end_seconds": 126.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "hmm, no, none that I know of"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.12,
      "end_seconds": 129.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "So, do you live alone?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.69,
      "end_seconds": 133.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Yes, I live on my own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.96,
      "end_seconds": 136.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "How about exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.7,
      "end_seconds": 140.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Not really, I don't get much exercise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.24,
      "end_seconds": 156.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "let me check your vitals now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.11,
      "end_seconds": 169.09,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "one second.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.99,
      "end_seconds": 194.71,
      "duration_seconds": 13.72,
      "text": "okay: weight 59 kilos, SpO2 98 percent on room air, temperature 36.7. And pressure 124 over 76, height 170 centimetres, BMI works out to 20.4, heart rate 73."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.86,
      "end_seconds": 200.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Okay, I need to examine you for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.55,
      "end_seconds": 203.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Take your time, no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.03,
      "end_seconds": 219.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "There's tenderness in the lower tummy on the left, and no guarding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.83,
      "end_seconds": 226.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "all done, you can get dressed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.97,
      "end_seconds": 247.58,
      "duration_seconds": 11.61,
      "text": "Putting it all together, this looks most like chronic pelvic pain, possibly endometriosis. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.83,
      "end_seconds": 254.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.42,
      "end_seconds": 264.32,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with chronic pelvic pain, possibly endometriosis do well once it's treated properly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.44,
      "end_seconds": 291.53,
      "duration_seconds": 14.09,
      "text": "I think a pelvic ultrasound makes sense here, for pelvic pain. Let's use mefenamic acid, 500 milligrams, three times a day with food, for five days. You take it by mouth. That's for period pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.59,
      "end_seconds": 296.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "okay, and I take that after food?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.22,
      "end_seconds": 316.36,
      "duration_seconds": 18.14,
      "text": "A heat pad and and some gentle movement help many people, and a pain diary helps me see a pattern. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.8,
      "end_seconds": 323.12,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Mm-hm. I'd like you to see a gynaecologist as well, and I'll write the referral."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.56,
      "end_seconds": 325.26,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.92,
      "end_seconds": 331.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "We'll catch up after the scan. Do you have any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.29,
      "end_seconds": 337.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "No, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}